[61/1873] FragilityIndex
# sentinel:claim-language-allow
TITLE: Fragility Index Calculator: Browser-Based Statistical Fragility for RCTs
TYPE: methods  |  ESTIMAND: Fragility Index (FI)
DATA: Six built-in landmark RCT datasets
PATH: C:\Models\FragilityIndex

CURRENT BODY (156 words):
Can a browser-based tool compute the Fragility Index and Fragility Quotient for randomized trials with binary outcomes without any software installation? We implemented the Walsh et al. (2014) algorithm, iteratively adding one event to the lower-rate arm until the two-sided Fisher exact p-value crosses 0.05, across six landmark datasets. The calculator uses exact Fisher tests with automatic direction detection, handling significant and non-significant trials through standard and reverse fragility indices. For DAPA-HF the Fragility Index is 62 and Fragility Quotient 1.31 percent, the two-sided Fisher p rising past 0.05 only at the sixty-second reassignment, computed in under 50 milliseconds. Sensitivity analysis across multiple thresholds confirmed the fragility index rose monotonically with the threshold across all six datasets wherever each trial remained significant. Browser-based fragility computation achieves outputs identical to dedicated R packages while eliminating every installation barrier. The limitation is that fragility indices apply only to binary outcomes analyzed with Fisher exact tests, excluding continuous endpoints.

YOUR REWRITE (at most 156 words, 7 sentences):


